WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.240
If you can dodge a wrench, you can dodge a
ball.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.540
DodgeBall came out in theaters in 2004 and
we've been quoting it since.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:11.990
While it's hard to believe that DodgeBall
came out nearly 15 years ago, let's take a

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.379
second to see where the movie's main players
find themselves nowadays.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.730
Vince Vaughn was already well-known for Swingers
and Old School when he starred in DodgeBall,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.110
but the film marked the beginning of a new
phase in Vaughn's career: that of big budget,

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.200
big screen comedies.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.040
The next year, he appeared in Wedding Crashers,
which solidified his status as a comedy leading

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.540
man.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.680
Vaughn's next movies included a number of
films that he also helped to write and produce,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.400
including The Break-Up, Couples Retreat, and
The Internship.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.320
He also reunited with DodgeBall co-star Ben
Stiller in The Watch.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.680
"Tell me about yourself.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.800
I know you got a wife.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.300
Have any kids?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:46.800
How old?"

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.940
"Zero years old.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:49.920
No kids."

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.000
Vaughn later took up more dramatic work, including
a starring role in True Detective Season 2.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.580
He also had a supporting role in Best Picture
nominee Hacksaw Ridge.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.320
His most recent roles veer toward "family"
entertainment, literally.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:08.220
He nabbed a recurring role as Chet Stevenson
on the Netflix animated comedy F is for Family.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.520
He also had a part in Fighting with My Family,
a movie about the rise of WWE star Paige.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.360
Ben Stiller has had a varied career as an
actor, writer, and director, and 2004 seemed

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.840
like a watershed year for him.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.960
While Stiller was already famous for Meet
the Parents and Zoolander, 2004 saw him starring

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.540
in hits Meet the Fockers, Starsky &amp; Hutch,
and Along Came Polly.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:34.920
He has continued to be hugely successful since,
lending his voice to the Madagascar series,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.740
appearing in the Night at the Museum franchise,
and writing, directing, and starring in Tropic

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.240
Thunder.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.620
He also appeared in The Meyerowitz Stories
opposite Adam Sandler, which got a standing

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.560
ovation at Cannes in 2017.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.600
He's also moved behind the camera and into
more dramatic work recently, producing and

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.130
directing the based-on-a-true-story prison
break miniseries Escape at Dannemora, which

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.260
earned 12 nominations at the 2019 Emmy Awards.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.900
Stiller hasn't forgotten his DodgeBall days.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.510
He recently organized a charity dodgeball
competition for his Ben Stiller Foundation

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.780
focused around the film.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.950
Stiller was able to reunite many of his co-stars
for the promo video, which gave fans the chance

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.560
to play dodgeball with him and his famous
friends.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.840
The game was played live on Today with the
anchors, fans, and Justin Long.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.080
Christine Taylor had a solid career on screen
before DodgeBall.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.560
She was best known for playing Marcia Brady
in two Brady Bunch movies.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.380
Other roles include parts in The Wedding Singer,
Zoolander, and The Craft.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:36.420
Following DodgeBall, she appeared in License
to Wed and more recently Little Boxes.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:41.280
Taylor has appeared in a number of projects
with Stiller over the years, including Zoolander,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.720
Tropic Thunder, and Arrested Development,
and with good reason.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:49.140
The two were married in 2000 after meeting
on the unaired pilot Heat Vision and Jack.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.940
The pair announced their separation in May
2017.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.240
Luckily, their split was amicable, so we can't
rule out them working together again someday.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.560
Justin Long earned himself a concussion from
his character's inability to dodge a ball,

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.820
but he also earned himself pretty lofty status
in Hollywood.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.540
DodgeBall marked one of his earliest roles
following small parts in Galaxy Quest and

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.320
Crossroads, but it was just the start for
the young star.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.100
He starred opposite Lindsay Lohan in Herbie:
Fully Loaded the following year.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.820
From there, he starred in a number of comedies
including The Break-Up and Accepted.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:26.180
He moved into action territory with Live Free
or Die Hard and went back to horror with Drag

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:26.840
Me to Hell.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.430
He also lent his voice to the Alvin and the
Chipmunks film trilogy series as the titular

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.620
troublemaking rodent.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.700
The role he's best known for, though?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:40.100
Playing Mac in Apple's "Get a Mac" ad campaign,
which ran from 2006 to 2009.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.740
Stephen Root unleashed his inner Hulk as Gordon
in DodgeBall.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.120
Best known for his playing Milton in Office
Space, the veteran character actor has kept

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.500
busy since DodgeBall.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.160
Shortly after the film was released, Root
appeared in the romantic comedy Just Friends.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.780
Root has found himself in small parts in many
high profile films.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.700
The actor has appeared in No Country For Old
Men, Selma, The Ballad Of Buster Scruggs and

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.200
more.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.220
He also had a part in the hit horror film
Get Out, playing gallery owner Jim Hudson.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.720
Root has also had an extensive career in television,
appearing on True Blood, 24, and Boardwalk

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.220
Empire.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:21.400
In the 90s he also gave life to two iconic
TV roles: angry boss Jimmy James on NewsRadio

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.600
and sad sack Bill on King of the Hill.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.960
In 2018, he landed the role of Monroe Fuches,
handler and mentor of the titular character

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.720
on Bill Hader's pitch-black hitman comedy
Barry.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.580
For his work in the show's second season,
Root received his first-ever Emmy nomination.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.580
Joel David Moore had an adorable love affair
with the other team in DodgeBall, and has

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.160
continued to charm audiences with his sweetness.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.639
DodgeBall was one of Moore's earliest roles,
but he quickly followed it up with slasher

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.580
Hatchet and the much-maligned The Hottie and
the Nottie.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:56.360
Moore has also been a consistent television
guest star, appearing on multiple episodes

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.910
of Bones, Medium, and in a supporting role
on the short-lived ABC drama series Forever.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.540
"Pure gold, 24 karat, unalloyed."

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:06.760
"Lucas, please."

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:07.260
"Sorry.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:07.760
Sorry."

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:12.100
You may also recognize him from his music
video appearances, with the actor starring

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.560
in videos from Fall Out Boy and Katy Perry.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:19.380
Moore's most notable role to date was as Norm
Spellman in James Cameron's Avatar.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.840
He'll be kept busy for the next few years
with the role, with Moore set to play Spellman

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.240
in all four of the planned Avatar sequels.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.199
Chris Williams was already an established
actor when he played Dwight in DodgeBall,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.580
and he continues to be a popular actor today.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:39.440
Williams followed up the film with guest appearances
on shows like Reno 911!, Monk, and Weeds.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:44.060
Williams landed recurring roles on shows like
Californication and Curb Your Enthusiasm.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.400
He recently starred as Eddie on The Great
Indoors, which was cancelled after just one

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:48.900
season.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:54.080
He also appears on Silicon Valley as Hoover,
the loyal assistant to evil tech boss Gavin

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:54.580
Belson.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.560
You'll recognize Steve the Pirate if you're
a fan of sci-fi, as actor Alan Tudyk was already

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.220
well-established as Wash in cult hit Firefly.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:08.180
Not long after DodgeBall, he played Wash again
in Firefly sequel film Serenity.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:13.490
Tudyk has had many high profile roles, with
appearances in 3:10 to Yuma, and Transformers:

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:14.060
Dark of the Moon.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.139
And in the final season of the Netflix zombie
comedy Santa Clarita Diet, Tudyk replaced

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:24.160
Firefly costar Nathan Fillion in the role
of Gary, a decomposing, disembodied head.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:29.180
You also heard Tudyk as the droid K-2SO in
Rogue One: A Star Wars Story.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:34.660
The actor has some prolific pipes, lending
his voice to huge films like Frozen, Zootopia,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.620
and Moana.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.980
Gary Cole played the straight man of the DodgeBall
commentating duo as Cotton McKnight.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.040
While you've likely seen Cole elsewhere on
the big screen, most famously as Bill Lumbergh

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.540
in Office Space, you're more likely to have
seen him on the small screen.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.600
He's had a prolific career as a guest star
on TV shows like Supernatural and 30 Rock.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.600
He's also had recurring roles on Entourage,
Suits, and Veep, the last of which got him

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.840
an Emmy nomination.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.260
Cole is also a well-known voice actor, who
has had prominent roles in properties like

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:08.260
Harvey Birdman: Attorney at Law, Kim Possible,
and Bob's Burgers.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:14.520
Jason Bateman delivered some of DodgeBall's
most memorable lines in his role as commentator

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.040
Pepper.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.820
"It's a bold strategy, Cotton, let's see if
it pays off for 'em."

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:23.759
The outlandish part was a huge departure from
his most notable role as straight man Michael

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.300
Bluth on Arrested Development.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:30.560
Few actors have racked up as lengthy a TV
resume as Bateman, who landed his first small

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.960
screen role in 1981, as James Cooper Ingalls
on Little House on the Prairie.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.780
He earned two Emmy nominations and won a Golden
Globe for Arrested Development, but he won

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.000
an Emmy in 2019 for directing an episode of
the stark crime drama Ozark.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.360
He also stars in the show as money launderer
Marty Byrde.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:52.020
Bateman also has many major movies parts,
including starring roles in the Horrible Bosses

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.380
series, and Game Night.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:59.280
The late Rip Torn portrayed mildly mad dodgeball
coach Patches O'Houlihan in DodgeBall, but

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:03.020
Hank Azaria played the character as a younger
man in a training video.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.600
Azaria has been a major part of some of the
biggest and funniest shows and movies of the

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.780
past three decades.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:14.460
He's been a utility voice actor on The Simpsons
since its inception, portraying, among others,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:19.920
Chief Wiggum, Moe, Carl, Superintendent Chalmers,
Comic Book Guy, and Kwik-E-Mart proprietor

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:20.420
Apu.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:26.560
In 2017, he turned Jim Brockmire, a baseball
announcer he played in a Funny or Die sketch,

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.660
into a full-length sitcom from IFC called
Brockmire.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.160
"We have run out of cheeks to turn, people!

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:34.220
We're fresh out of 'em!"

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:39.620
Azaria also portrayed Gargamel in two big-screen
Smurfs movies, while enjoying a recurring

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.340
role on Showtime's Ray Donovan.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.140
While dodgeball isn't a real professional
sport, filmmakers managed to keep the playing

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:50.400
sequences as realistic and above board as
possible.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:55.180
Portraying the tournament referee in the film's
climactic showdown, we've got Al Kaplon, an

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:58.100
actor and real-life minor league baseball
umpire.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:02.740
Kaplon called balls and strikes for a decade
as an official before turning to acting.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:07.420
He first played, what else, an umpire in the
baseball movie Talent for the Game.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:12.120
He followed that up with small parts on episodes
of The X-Files and the sports-themed sitcom

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.180
Inside Schwartz.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.640
He also did commercials for Toyota and Nike.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:21.180
He played the Memorial Field umpire in 61*,
an HBO movie about Roger Marist's home run

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:21.680
chase.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.560
At least he got to call something other than
baseball in DodgeBall.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:30.740
Following that high-profile gig, he was named
the head referee on NBC's short-lived revival

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.300
of American Gladiators.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:37.740
Following small roles in S.W.A.T. and The
Rundown, DodgeBall was Jamal Duff's third

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:42.640
movie, and the actor portrayed Me'Shell Jones,
dodgeball monster and loyal second-in-command

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.400
to White Goodman.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.340
Duff strikes an imposing figure in real life,
too.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:52.320
The 6'7" actor played as a defensive end and
defensive tackle in the NFL in the 1990s.

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:57.680
He also played for the Los Angeles Xtreme,
league champions in the old XFL's one-and-only

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.180
season.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.240
And in the 2000s, he decided to give acting
a shot.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:07.220
After DodgeBall, Duff booked dozens of roles
in movies and TV shows, often playing bouncers,

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.480
guards, or just general tough guys.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:14.660
This includes a security guard on Future Man
and "Tough Guy #1" on an episode of Fresh

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:15.460
Off the Boat.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:21.320
His most high-profile work to date is a recurring
role as Zeke on Brooklyn Nine-Nine, the brother-in-law

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.320
of Terry Jeffords.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:27.840
Like her on-screen DodgeBall love interest
Justin Long, Julie Gonzalo was well into her

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.780
20s when she portrayed a teenager, specifically
cheerleader Amber.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:36.760
Around the time of DodgeBall's release in
2004, Gonzalo played a lot of teens, such

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.470
as in Freaky Friday and A Cinderella Story.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:45.040
In 2006, Gonzalo scored her biggest early
career role, as Hearst College student Parker

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.020
Lee on the third season of cult classic Veronica
Mars.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:53.320
Gonzalo is also well-known for her role as
Pamela Rebecca Barnes on TNT's Dallas sequel

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:53.820
series.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:59.500
Along with guest star gigs on series ranging
from Castle to CSI: Miami to Grey's Anatomy,

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:04.730
Gonzalo landed one other major role on a short-lived
show, playing attorney Maggie Dekker in legal

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.440
dramedy Eli Stone.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:11.300
Even if you've seen DodgeBall hundreds of
times, you probably wouldn't be able to pick

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.960
Missi Pyle out of a line-up.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:18.580
The gorgeous actress made a huge transformation
for the part of Globo Gym player Fran, going

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:22.460
from blonde to dark brunette and adding in
a unibrow for good measure.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.840
Since DodgeBall, Pyle has gone back to her
normal self, but she's had good luck as a

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.720
character actress throughout her career.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:33.320
Shortly after DodgeBall, Pyle played Violet's
overbearing mother in Charlie and the Chocolate

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:33.820
Factory.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.380
She later appeared in Gone Girl and Jumanji:
Welcome to the Jungle.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:42.060
Pyle has popped up all over the small screen,
including appearances on sketch comedy show

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:47.370
Inside Amy Schumer, Netflix original Lady
Dynamite, and CBS primetime anchor Two and

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.020
a Half Men.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.400
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:54.100
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:58.100
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

